{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants","id":631116,"title":"World Convenants?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-18T06:57:38-07:00","id":631116,"title":"World Convenants?","content":"Has anyone ever considered the possibility of covenants originated from around the world rather than the usual five?<br /> <br /> For example, covenants originated from East and Southern Asia that are Taoist, Shinto, Hindu, Buddhist, Jainist, Sikh, based?<br /> <br /> Also what about Convenants originated from south western asia that are based on Judahism, Islam, Mesopotamian religions, etc?<br /> <br /> Also what about Convenants originated from Africa such as based on Egyptian Religion in East Africa and such?<br /> <br /> Well lastly what about Pre-Columbian Kindred who have covenants based on Mesoamerican and Pre-Columbian North American religions as well?<br /> <br /> Or hell what about Covenants originated from Northern Western Asia (Europe) that are Ancient Greek, Norse, Slavic, Celtic, Basque, Germanic, Etruscan, etc based?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","user":"Black Blood","date":". 08-18-2015, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:45:59-07:00","id":631173,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the religious ones were variants of the Circle of the Crone or the Lancea et Sanctum. It goes into detail about them in their corresponding covenant book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:15:31-07:00","id":631197,"title":"","content":"One of the Bloodlines books has a few different covenants from around the world in it. There's a Thai covenant of vampire Buddhists attempting to work off the karma of the Curse, a Japanese Amaterasu cult, an Indian caste system that equates clans with varnas, and a few other things. It's a bit fuzzy, it's been years since I've read the book, but it's got some good plunder in it for that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:34:00-07:00","id":631407,"title":"","content":"Always loved the Amanotsukai to Death.<br /> <br /> Their currently under the Aegis of the Crone.<br /> <br /> But thats largely out of ease of categorization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T12:58:30-07:00","id":631449,"title":"","content":"Maybe perhaps the <a href=\"https://authorlyngibson.wordpress.com/2014/05/01/the-jumlin-a-vampire-legend-from-the-cherokee-nation/\" target=\"_blank\">Legend of Jumlin</a> should be used for Pre-Columbian Kindred perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7348-black-blood","name":"Black Blood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T13:05:30-07:00","id":631451,"title":"","content":"Its not only a good idea, its assumed by the setting that such things exist.<br /> <br /> But I would refrain from simply making cultural/religious Covenants. That's both a limiting view on the concept of Covenant and on the very cultures you will base them.<br /> <br /> Think about what people in a given region will find relevant to work for. A person in Egypt won't look for a Covenant based on being Egyptian. Its kind of expected that almost everyone will be Egyptian in Egypt, anyway, that isn't relevant. But there you have some sort of conflict between Egyptian Revivalists and Orthodox Muslims. So a Covenant based on cultural revivalism without the religious side would be found there, and another similar to the Lancea, but following Islam.<br /> <br /> Regional Covenants should focus on regional politics, not in being just regional. That's, though, IS a thing among IMMIGRANTS. On Texas you could have a Covenant based on Mexico and being Mexican, or generally being Latin-american, because it is a thing there. On New York City you could have a bunch of minor Covenants based on diverse cultures, like Irish and Chinese, and as time passed some of those coalesced into two or three somewhat conflicting Covenants, or just one Covenant based on being an Immigrant.<br /> <br /> Lots of possibilities are given. In the end, the Covenants present in a given city should work the themes and conflicts of the city. And sure, some of them can be very distinct of the most known Covenants, and even be based on specific cultures. If for some reason half a dozen of the Egyptian Orthodox Muslim Vampires migrate to, lets say, Vancouver, so you would have their Covenant in Vancouver. And though they define themselves by being Muslims, the Covenant would be strongly modern-Egyptian &quot;themed&quot; simply because it was founded and is mainly composed by Egyptian vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:01:34-07:00","id":631531,"title":"","content":"2e does away with the need to fold literally everything into versions of the main five Covenants and both explicitly states and showcases that there are all sorts of Covenants across the world, the big five are merely the most common ones.<br /> <br /> Hong Kong has its Ministries, for instance, and the Margraviate of Berlin has its own, too. Tokyo has a very distinct set up that differs significantly from the western cities, with Kindred having set up themselves as <i>zaibatsu</i> with their own concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T14:02:05-07:00","id":631535,"title":"","content":"Here's what I've picked/speculated from the second edition:<br /> <br /> Eastern Asia: <i>Blood and Smoke </i>mentions some in Beijing and Tokyo. <i>Requiem for Regina</i> surprisingly put Invictus in the Far East, while <i>Blood and Smoke</i> referred to Ventrue empires with little more detail.<br /> <br /> Pre-Columbian America: The Mission in San Francisco is Native American in all but name and trappings. That's not to mention <i>Shadows of Mexico</i>, although that's described as one hoary side of the Circle of the Crone there, albeit one which had as much in common with Invictus in its heyday.<br /> <br /> Europe (but mostly the British Isles): There are two ancient cults in Athens that correspond to the Lancea et Sanctum and the Circle. The former is recognises Apollo as well as the Christian god by the looks of it, but they don't accept the Lancea et Sanctum proper. The latter might not have actually contacted the Circle of the Crone as a movement before. As well as the presumably extinct Gallows Post and children's crusade, <i>Requiem for Regina</i> briefly describes:<br /> *the Weihan Cynn - in spite of their Anglo-Saxon name (which was used in London, but not Edinburgh where it remained stronger), they were in Britain when the Roman came. They make deals with various other supernaturals.<br /> *the Qalandariyyah - an originally Muslim sect from Andalusia that operates within the above.<br /> *the Fuil-Beannaithe - An Irish cult that reveres the Virgin Mary and supports Catholicism within Britain, but also incorporates beliefs from the New World.<br /> <br /> Those may be extinct or drawn into the Circle of Crone now, but they were around as late as the early 18th century. I'm guessing that the Lancea et Sanctum managed to almost wipe them out in the late 18th/early 19th century before a massive counter attack. I would imagine that the Circle of the Crone has soaked up a lot of Western pagan traditions for the sake of solidarity (even ones that don't recognise any crone figure or value tribulation or Cruac), but is near unheard of in places where the Lancea et Sanctum was never strong enough to persecute other cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T12:50:19-07:00","id":633719,"title":"","content":"I have an Egyptian Covenant, ancient but static, and could certainly believe there are fairly localized covenants worldwide. I have a group that I'm on the fence as to whether they are an Order (such as what flourishes in the Invictus) or a Covenant in their own right. Really, depending on how Covenants interact between Domains in your setting, an Invictus member in Toronto may have little inherent status among the Invictus in Buenos Aires or Lisbon -- indeed, she may barely recognize the Covenant culture there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:14:19-07:00","id":634675,"title":"","content":"I'm working on a covenant based on the social structures of the Sasanian (Persian) Empire. The idea is that Persian vampires would be highly resistant to adopting the social structures of the Invictus and the Lance because of the long history of conflict between Greco-Roman culture and the Persians. Called '<span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u0112r\u0101nshahr' this covenant would control modern day Iran and some of the surrounding territories. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T13:20:15-07:00","id":636220,"title":"","content":"For a single Covenant to control a vast territory, it is more likely to be a cultural background for local vampires than an actual Covenant, unless you see reason for those vampires to form a political construct like a Covenant.<br /> <br /> In the least, I see such Covenant as being similar to the Invictus in its role in the area, even if without contact with the Invictus proper or even at odds with them.<br /> <br /> The Covenants only make sense at all in regard to one another. A place with only one of them actually have none.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:35:21-07:00","id":645960,"title":"","content":"Yeah, in a very long running game me and 4 other players started our own covenant based on Egyptian lore and customs. Game took place in the ancient times and when we went back to playing modern day it was there but on a smaller scale than other covenants. After that we started making it grow and its now the leading covenant in (of all places) Dublin. Fun stuff lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7529-silentstaccato","name":"SilentStaccato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7529_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T18:51:14-07:00","id":646178,"title":"","content":"I really want to run a span-across-the-centuries game someday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-25T13:52:13-07:00","id":677939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants?p=646178#post646178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really want to run a span-across-the-centuries game someday.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those can be tricky in VtR. What my group has done is fold in narratives from previous games into each of the games. We hop around the centuries doing a lot of peroid mini-games (3 to 5 sessions) and if we can find a way to reference a previous time peroid we do. <br /> <br /> As for non-european covenants, we've done those to one degree or another. We use Followers of Set whenever we touch on North Africa/Middle East. In our end of bronze age game they controlled from Algeria to the Fertile Crescent. In Modern Nighs, they only hold sway in Egypt and Sudan. <br /> <br /> During our Mongol game had a this freaky Mongolian Bhuddist covenant with a kind of broken discipline that let you talk to Spirits of the Shadow. Old Mongolian Bhuddism is riff with demons and spirits (not what westerners are pitched) and this covenant was all about bargaining and placating them (for profit of course).<br /> <br /> There's a Coil of the Dragon like tradition called Treasures of Mai Jing that we folded into Taoism and made a semi-religious convenant has deep roots in South East Asia. <br /> <br /> We also had something that looks alot like the Gallows out of Blood and Smoke. It was this covenant that was a network of waystations/hostels in South East Asian islands. It had a shark motif and it was sort of Circle of the Crone and sort of Carthian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1031-youvegotwildtalents","name":"youvegotwildtalents","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T03:17:49-07:00","id":680850,"title":"","content":"In theory, the book says there are other covenants out there, across the world, that are different from the core seven (including Brood/VII). They're each unique. Even in the US, we have several that are different.<br /> <br /> In practice? I rarely see a new covenant that's not just tweaking the history and a few of the practices of the core seven. Call the Buddhist organization that learns Treasures a different covenant all you want, but in execution, the mechanics and themes are still very close to the Ordo Dracul. Vodoun religion in Ancient Bloodlines has much in common with the other religious covenant. Same with the new covenants in Danse Macabre - each could easily fit as a variant of the established groups. The four Zaibatsu in Tokyo might as well just be labeled as localized Carthians, Invictus, Circle, and VII with slightly different mechanics.<br /> <br /> Politically, culturally and historically, these various covenants are not the same. Thematically and mechanically, we're so close we might as well be the same for others. Unlike Mage, Vampire is a tier 2 game, which means that we don't have global organizations, but the covenant archetypes remain pretty much the same. So, if we look at a game in southern Africa, I'd expect to see the Lancea reformed into an extreme Muslim-based group with similar mechanics, a CotC equivalent that is based on Yoruba and other local religions, likely an Invictus epoxy that's left behind as a result of colonialism, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:32:11-07:00","id":682204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants?p=680850#post680850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In practice? I rarely see a new covenant that's not just tweaking the history and a few of the practices of the core seven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely, though, my answer to this is who cares? Because I think the first part of this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Politically, culturally and historically, these various covenants are not the same. Thematically and mechanically, we're so close we might as well be the same for others. </div> </div> </div>... outweighs the second, especially when we're talking about immortals, even the punctuated immortality the Kindred have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Call the Buddhist organization that learns Treasures a different covenant all you want, but in execution, the mechanics and themes are still very close to the Ordo Dracul. </div> </div> </div>I can't find the post that made this case, but there was some who argued (very strongly) that a Buddhist covenant would act more like the Lancea Sanctum than the Ordo Dracul - though unlike the Lancea, their condition wouldn't be permanent, and they could look forward to reincarnation as a human later on if they performed their lives well. But Theban Sorcery would be hella inappropriate for them (Treasures might be better, but are too suggestive of the idea that every Buddhist thinks this life is the one where they'll get Nirvana, which for the hungry dead, is a preposterous notion).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd expect to see the Lancea reformed into an extreme Muslim-based group with similar mechanics, a CotC equivalent that is based on Yoruba and other local religions, likely an Invictus epoxy that's left behind as a result of colonialism, etc. </div> </div> </div>There was a thread on Muslim covenants where the idea came up that rather than something Theban Sorcery like, they'd have a power that's more Carthian Law like - enforcing the legal interpretations of the covenant's imams.<br /> <br /> I don't know about Yoruba religion in particular, but Cruac and the Circle are based around the idea of blood as a conduit between the earthly and the divine - while that's a common mystical notion, it's not universal, and where it doesn't hold, blood is likely to be considered a <i>barrier</i> - and becoming a vampire has no reason to change that (blood is after all, even more blatantly bound to sustaining a vampire's earthly life; and it comes more easily than food and is less of a loss to the vampire than a human's blood, making it a pretty paltry offering). For example, in Japan, I'd be expecting the Shinto-esque covenant, if there is one, to be the last that would use blood in its rites or learn Cruac. (But again, Theban Sorcery or a Lancea Sanctum like attitude wouldn't make sense either).<br /> <br /> None of these changes are very big, and mostly consist of shuffling the existing elements around. But I don't think it needs any more than that to make something worth calling a new covenant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T03:48:09-07:00","id":684210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants?p=682204#post682204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Largely, though, my answer to this is who cares? Because I think the first part of this:<br /> ... outweighs the second, especially when we're talking about immortals, even the punctuated immortality the Kindred have.</div> </div> </div> </div> *Shrugs* From a meta-level design stage, I don't consider them to be different covenants. Snake charmer Sanctified have a different history and culture than the standard Catholic LS, and yet they're the same covenant. To me, its all just a matter of semantics and degrees at this point. It all depends on where you draw the line, and that depends on STs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of these changes are very big, and mostly consist of shuffling the existing elements around. But I don't think it needs any more than that to make something worth calling a new covenant. </div> </div> </div> See? You're just arguing about what you consider the line to cross. &quot;I consider this line new!&quot; &quot;Well, I consider that line new!&quot; &quot;No THIS is the line over here!&quot; No one agrees on the line. <br /> <br /> Now, if you made up an entirely new set of benefits, with an entirely new set of belief structures and philosphy as well as history and culture, then we'd all be talking about a new covenant. As it is? I'm just see everything you said as a semantics argument over the word &quot;new.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:33:37-07:00","id":684252,"title":"","content":"But does Buddhist vampires have anything to Ordo Dracul then beside the Coils, history wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:39:54-07:00","id":684255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants?p=684210#post684210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *Shrugs* From a meta-level design stage, I don't consider them to be different covenants. Snake charmer Sanctified have a different history and culture than the standard Catholic LS, and yet they're the same covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, why do history and culture matter less than which funky Discipline they get?<br /> <br /> Or: say you have a Middle Eastern group consisting of Islamic (or quasi-Islamic) scholars who consider the Kindred rather than the Djinn to be the &quot;other people&quot; referred to in the Qu'ran, and debate and make judgements about how Kindred should engage with the law and the world - are they Carthians just because you use Carthian Law systems to represent the metaphysical force of their edicts - or are they Lancea because they worship the Abrahamic God, even though they don't act as scourges of the living, or accept the event or metaphysics from which the Lancea takes its name, and don't consider themselves irretrievably damned - or are they Invictus because they assume a position of general power to determine bounds for all vampires - or are they new?<br /> <br /> Buddhist mythology holds the hungry dead to be tormentors of the living as an object lesson to both - are a group that base themselves around this belief the Lancea, even though they don't believe in the Abrahamic God, have an entirely different view of what &quot;damnation&quot; and &quot;purpose&quot; mean, and don't consider their condition eternal - or would allowing them to learn something akin to the Coils to mitigate their crap a little make them the Ordo Dracul, even though to them the Coils-alike are a means of coming to terms with their state rather than a stepping stone to evolving into another, and rather than a unique transcendence, they look forward to the same chance of reincarnation everyone gets - or are they new?<br /> <br /> The Carthians are to a large extent defined negatively: that is, they're the political groupings that are different from the Invictus, lumped together because the Invictus is big, powerful, and monolithic enough to have all political groups measured against it - nonetheless, Carthian groups can be as different from one another as they are from the Invictus . So what about regions where the Invictus doesn't hold the same cultural sway, and doesn't provide the same reason to lump all the not-Invictus together? Would it then make sense to still do so?<br /> <br /> The Gallows Post is explicitly defined as a separate covenant. Suppose a similar group was still extant in the desert cities of Central Asia - a place where travel was even harder, trade lifeblood, and merchants critical enough to grant them an esteem most historical cultures didn't - vampires whose function was social glue, brokerage, conveyance, and general middle-manning (between other covenants and other places), also using Blood Oaths to guarantee good faith on all sides? Are they Invictus, Gallows Post, or new?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See? You're just arguing about what you consider the line to cross. </div> </div> </div>And?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it is? I'm just see everything you said as a semantics argument over the word &quot;new.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 10-01-2015, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T04:43:52-07:00","id":684258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Blood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/631116-world-convenants#post631116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever considered the possibility of covenants originated from around the world rather than the usual five?<br /> <br /> For example, covenants originated from East and Southern Asia that are Taoist, Shinto, Hindu, Buddhist, Jainist, Sikh, based?<br /> <br /> Also what about Convenants originated from south western asia that are based on Judahism, Islam, Mesopotamian religions, etc?<br /> <br /> Also what about Convenants originated from Africa such as based on Egyptian Religion in East Africa and such?<br /> <br /> Well lastly what about Pre-Columbian Kindred who have covenants based on Mesoamerican and Pre-Columbian North American religions as well?<br /> <br /> Or hell what about Covenants originated from Northern Western Asia (Europe) that are Ancient Greek, Norse, Slavic, Celtic, Basque, Germanic, Etruscan, etc based?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the covenants listed in the book are just supposed to be the major power structures known in the western world, but it hints at the existence of other covenants as well. Like Seven and Belial's Brood. Like many things in the book, they're just examples to help give you ideas. You're free to add, remove, or rewrite new content depending on your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}